ursion and stack overflow\" (PY7: the C"] [1310 3 "// level's check, test_isinstance's test_isinstance_recursion_limit overflowed Go's stack)"] [1362 33 "// _PyUnion_Check: its arguments as a tuple"] [1366 58 "// object_issubclass's (PY7)"] [1405 1 "// checkClass is check_class: o's __bases__ a tuple, else the TypeError msg; an error other than AttributeError"] [1406 1 "// getting it raised as it is (PY7: it became the TypeError)."] [1418 1 "// abstractIsSubclass is abstract_issubclass: c's __bases__ walked, an error other than AttributeError raised"] [1419 1 "// (PY7: it was dropped), the C level's check before each recursion (test_isinstance's"] [1420 1 "// test_infinite_recursion_via_bases_tuple and test_infinite_cycle_in_bases overflowed Go's stack)."] [1455 1 "// posArgs checks a built-in's positional argument count, CPython's messages."] [1473 1 "// ---- object's pickling protocol (typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex__, reduce_newobj, object_getstate) ----"] [1475 1 "// importModule is __import__(name) through the interpreter's builtins (PY5e's import system)."] [1484 1 "// importErrorType is ImportError when the runtime has it, else RuntimeError."] [1500 1 "// objectGetState is object.__getstate__: the instance's __dict__ (None when empty), with its"] [1501 1 "// __slots__' values as a second dictionary."] [1520 3 "// the basic size's check: a built-in base's fields, or slots the names do not cover, cannot be saved"] [1554 1 "// typeSlotNames is _PyType_GetSlotNames: the class's __slotnames__, else copyreg._slotnames's answer; nil for none."] [1615 2 "// reduce_newobj: a state is required of what its arguments, items and pairs do not rebuild"] [1638 1 "// selfMethod puts a built-in method that takes a subclass's instance itself in t's dictionary."] [1644 2 "// object_getstate: object's own __getstate__ with the required check, any other called"] [1653 2 "// set_reduce, deque_reduce, bytearray's _common_reduce: type(self), its items, the state"] [1690 2 "// method_reduce: getattr(self, name)"] [1699 2 "// object___sizeof__: tp_basicsize, here the header's two words"] [1710 3 "// typeobject.c's object___reduce_ex___impl: a __reduce__ overriding object's, a built-in type's too"] [1739 1 "// BuiltinValue is the built-in value an instance of a class deriving from a built-in type carries"] [1740 1 "// (a list subclass's list), else o itself: for the core types' functions taking their subclasses."] [1743 1 "// builtinHasDict is a built-in type's tp_dictoffset: it, or a built-in type it derives from, shows a __dict__."] [1753 1 "// builtinHasWeak is a built-in type's tp_weaklistoffset, for the types one can derive from (CPython's that have a"] [1754 1 "// weak list; types.GenericAlias's since the merge with queue 225: typing's aliases are its subclasses)."] [1771 1 "// varSized is a type's tp_itemsize: its instances hold their items after the header, so that a class deriving"] [1772 1 "// from it can add no __slots__ and no __weakref__ (type has an itemsize too, and its own weak list)."] [1781 1 "// newSlots is type_new_slots over __slots__ (sl nil: none): the class's own slot names, sorted as"] [1782 1 "// type_new_copy_slots sorts them, and what it adds."] [1786 2 "// 3.15 (type_new_slots, gh-41779; queue 237): a variable-size base (tuple, int, bytes) takes any __slots__, and"] [1787 2 "// __weakref__ among them; its subclass without __slots__ still adds no weak reference"] [1809 2 "// type_new_slots_impl's check: identifiers, __dict__ and __weakref__ once"] [1831 2 "// 3.15's type_new_descriptors: custom slots on a variable-size base only for a tuple subclass (type's keeps 3.14's"] [1832 2 "// refusal: pyi's classes have no slots on a metaclass's instances)"] [1847 2 "// type_new_copy_slots"] [1857 5 "// CPython puts these names in the namespace itself: they leave it below"] [1865 2 "// type_new_slots_bases: a secondary base's __dict__ and __weakref__ come along"] [1882 1 "// addLayoutDescrs is type_add_getset of what the clas